WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.480
<b>General Affairs Office</b>

00:01.400 --> 00:04.250
All right, thank you for taking care of it.

00:04.250 --> 00:05.880
One more thing, Katase-san.

00:07.360 --> 00:08.610
Here's a little something...

00:09.240 --> 00:11.770
It's for everyone in Product Development.

00:13.030 --> 00:15.210
Thank you so much!

00:17.670 --> 00:20.070
Cookies, cookies...

00:21.620 --> 00:24.490
Sweet and yummy...

00:31.520 --> 00:32.970
I am exhausted.

00:33.590 --> 00:38.140
So much to do and learn 
when you're new...

00:38.140 --> 00:40.030
Shinozaki-san.

00:40.030 --> 00:41.390
S-Senpai?!

00:41.890 --> 00:43.400
Taking a break?

00:43.400 --> 00:44.640
Y-Yes.

00:45.100 --> 00:48.250
<i>Should I have told her first?</i>

00:48.250 --> 00:51.400
S-Sorry, I'll get right back to work—

00:53.600 --> 00:55.860
Um...

00:56.740 --> 00:57.780
Senpai?

01:01.460 --> 01:03.370
Shinozaki-san.

01:03.370 --> 01:05.370
Y-Yes?

01:06.530 --> 01:09.750
Which do you prefer: bears or bunnies?

01:12.480 --> 01:15.630
Which is it? Bears or bunnies?

01:17.090 --> 01:19.200
Bears or bunnies...?

01:19.200 --> 01:21.160
Right. Which is it?

01:21.840 --> 01:24.650
I-If I had to choose, bears, I think...

01:24.650 --> 01:25.770
Understood.

01:26.320 --> 01:27.350
Here!

01:28.410 --> 01:29.400
What is this?

01:30.400 --> 01:32.470
A little pick-me-up.

01:32.470 --> 01:36.420
People tend to get peckish 
and run-down around this time.

01:36.420 --> 01:40.160
Someone from general affairs gave these to me,

01:40.540 --> 01:43.660
and I'm going to share them 
with everyone else later on...

01:43.660 --> 01:47.110
But you get yours early, Shinozaki-san!

01:49.030 --> 01:51.920
Just don't tell anyone, okay?

01:53.820 --> 01:58.100
<i>There's a senpai where I work... 
who is tiny and cute.</i>

02:10.940 --> 02:15.700
My Tiny Senpai

03:28.970 --> 03:32.980
#02 Despite Appearances, I'm More the Big Sister Type.

03:32.040 --> 03:34.170
Good morning.

03:37.230 --> 03:39.740
I guess I'm first in, today.

03:44.620 --> 03:46.060
Aw...

03:48.640 --> 03:50.370
Good morning.

03:53.440 --> 03:57.430
Senpai never leaves her stuff 
on her desk like that.

03:58.840 --> 04:01.820
G-Good morning...

04:02.340 --> 04:04.360
S-S-Senpai?!

04:04.360 --> 04:05.260
Yes.

04:05.600 --> 04:07.280
What are you doing?!

04:07.280 --> 04:09.530
I... just...

04:09.530 --> 04:11.270
dropped this pen...

04:11.270 --> 04:13.290
Let me get out of your way!

04:13.290 --> 04:15.400
I'd appreciate that.

04:16.460 --> 04:17.400
Senpa...

04:27.860 --> 04:29.790
<i>Senpai's breasts!</i>

04:30.790 --> 04:33.720
Sorry! I'm so sorry! Let me move right now!

04:32.690 --> 04:35.290
You don't have to panic! It's okay!

04:40.670 --> 04:43.170
What a lovely morning you two are having.

04:43.170 --> 04:47.120
I-It's not what you think! 
It's just a coincidence!

04:48.290 --> 04:50.180
You, too, Hayakawa?!

04:50.670 --> 04:53.060
I think that dirty thoughts are bad.

04:53.440 --> 04:57.740
Seriously, it's just a coincidence!

05:01.990 --> 05:05.500
Senpai, were the documents I submitted okay?

05:06.270 --> 05:09.580
Give me a second and I can check.

05:14.030 --> 05:14.830
What the—?!

05:15.890 --> 05:17.620
Did I mess up?

05:17.930 --> 05:19.900
These documents...

05:22.750 --> 05:25.130
You did a really good job!

05:26.630 --> 05:27.870
Good boy!

05:27.870 --> 05:30.760
U-Um, Senpai...?

05:30.760 --> 05:33.270
Very, very good.

05:33.270 --> 05:34.300
Senpai...

05:34.300 --> 05:36.990
<i>My subordinates at work get along very well.</i>

05:35.160 --> 05:37.210
You worked hard, huh?

05:36.990 --> 05:38.270
<i>Honestly...</i>

05:38.270 --> 05:40.470
It's not that big a deal...

05:38.840 --> 05:43.000
<i>Would an ordinary pair of 
coworkers get along like that?</i>

05:40.470 --> 05:43.780
I never want to miss 
a chance to offer praise!

05:43.000 --> 05:44.780
<i>It feels a little more significant than that.</i>

05:45.190 --> 05:47.370
<i>More than coworkers, it's like they're...</i>

05:52.680 --> 05:54.660
Scouting a location for a drinking party?

05:54.660 --> 05:59.920
Right. I was supposed to go, 
but something came up kind of abruptly.

05:59.920 --> 06:02.360
Sure, I can do that.

06:02.360 --> 06:04.670
What a relief. Please do.

06:05.050 --> 06:09.800
And since the more opinions, the better, 
why don't you join him, Katase-san?

06:09.800 --> 06:12.740
Yay, I'd love to!

06:16.130 --> 06:18.300
I wonder what kind of place it is.

06:18.300 --> 06:20.690
I hope the food is tasty!

06:22.750 --> 06:25.130
It's supposed to be 
the top floor of this building.

06:25.130 --> 06:26.910
This should be fun!

06:26.910 --> 06:31.050
Since our manager chose it, 
I bet it's pretty fancy.

06:32.210 --> 06:35.700
I know what you mean, 
the night view is bound to be pretty.

06:33.130 --> 06:35.700
<i>Good, smooth sailing so far...</i>

06:36.340 --> 06:38.960
<i>Now they just need to keep it up, 
after going into the restaurant.</i>

06:39.480 --> 06:43.460
I think I might be a little drunk...

06:43.460 --> 06:45.550
S-Senpai...

06:48.650 --> 06:50.540
I'm not letting you go home tonight.

06:51.220 --> 06:53.560
I wouldn't want to.

06:56.970 --> 06:59.370
Shinozaki-san, I...

06:59.370 --> 07:01.750
Senpai... I...

07:05.840 --> 07:10.000
<i>That was a close one. 
I almost let my own fantasy fry my brain.</i>

07:10.000 --> 07:10.940
Manager?

07:11.960 --> 07:12.940
Hayakawa-san?!

07:12.940 --> 07:17.290
I thought you said you had 
sudden business to attend to?

07:22.660 --> 07:24.760
Oh, I get it.

07:24.760 --> 07:26.840
You're curious, too, aren't you, Hayakawa-san?

07:26.840 --> 07:28.510
He's your childhood friend, and coworker...

07:28.830 --> 07:30.510
Wait, no!

07:32.820 --> 07:34.510
<i>How could I be so cruel?!</i>

07:35.090 --> 07:38.720
If you need anything, you know who to ask.

07:38.560 --> 07:42.020
m 0 0 l 118 0 l 118 166 l 0 166

07:38.560 --> 07:42.020
<b>The age-gap
romance
between
a senpai
and kohai
at work.</b>

07:38.720 --> 07:42.020
<i>The age-gap romance 
between a senpai and kohai at work.</i>

07:42.020 --> 07:46.960
It's not like I ever really liked you 
all this time, or anything, Shinozaki!

07:46.440 --> 07:50.110
m 0 0 l 118 0 l 118 168 l 0 168

07:46.440 --> 07:50.110
<b>Or the
reunited
childhood
friends/
classmates
romance.</b>

07:46.960 --> 07:50.110
<i>Or the reunited childhood 
friends/classmates romance.</i>

07:50.110 --> 07:53.150
Which should I be rooting for?!

07:53.150 --> 07:57.030
Why am I even included?! 
I don't need that kind of support!

07:57.030 --> 07:58.970
What, really?

07:58.970 --> 08:02.680
Seriously, Shinozaki and I just go way back!

08:02.680 --> 08:03.630
Seriously?

08:03.630 --> 08:04.540
Seriously.

08:04.960 --> 08:07.180
I see...

08:07.180 --> 08:09.050
Why do you seem disappointed?

08:09.050 --> 08:11.870
Well, be that as it may,

08:11.870 --> 08:15.200
since you're here anyway, 
you should join me. Let's go!

08:14.430 --> 08:15.550
Wha...

08:16.060 --> 08:19.910
You have reservations, correct? 
We're pleased to have you.

08:20.430 --> 08:21.720
Right this way.

08:23.060 --> 08:25.090
Sneak, sneak, sneak...

08:25.090 --> 08:26.900
How did I get roped into this?

08:30.390 --> 08:32.160
Please, have a seat.

08:32.160 --> 08:35.820
These are our special tables 
that let you enjoy the night view.

08:36.350 --> 08:39.830
I'll be back for your order in a bit.

08:40.930 --> 08:44.580
<i>How's that? Getting dropped into those 
couples seats must be pretty exciting, right?</i>

08:45.040 --> 08:48.090
This should bring 
the two of them closer together, and...

08:48.490 --> 08:51.400
Not a lot of restaurants 
with side-by-side seating.

08:51.400 --> 08:52.590
<i>He didn't catch on!</i>

08:52.590 --> 08:55.480
This menu is huge, I don't know where to start.

08:55.480 --> 08:56.840
<i>She's focused on food!</i>

08:56.840 --> 08:59.390
I've never eaten somewhere like this before.

08:59.390 --> 09:01.180
Neither have I.

09:01.180 --> 09:04.410
It's what I'd expect from our manager, 
though. He's really got style.

09:04.410 --> 09:08.230
<i>They're not getting what I was going for, 
but they seem happy, so I guess it's okay?!</i>

09:08.680 --> 09:10.910
You're really enjoying this, Manager.

09:10.910 --> 09:12.480
You bet I am!

09:13.440 --> 09:14.480
You see...

09:16.630 --> 09:18.120
The thing is...

09:20.440 --> 09:24.870
Nothing makes me happier than 
cheering on someone else's love life.

09:27.160 --> 09:30.750
<i>I think our boss might be a weirdo.</i>

09:30.750 --> 09:32.800
This is rough, though...

09:32.800 --> 09:35.470
I thought the couples seating 
would get their pulses pounding.

09:35.470 --> 09:38.730
Oh, check it out, Senpai. Over there!

09:39.240 --> 09:40.510
What is it?

09:41.020 --> 09:43.930
That's our office right there, isn't it?

09:43.930 --> 09:46.770
Where?! I want to see!

10:01.030 --> 10:04.900
I knew it! It's easier to see from up here!

10:05.980 --> 10:09.080
S-Senpai... s-so close...

10:09.080 --> 10:10.540
a-and her....

10:10.540 --> 10:13.550
b-b-boobs are...!

10:15.120 --> 10:17.050
Is everything okay?

10:17.050 --> 10:19.610
Yes, it's a nice view...

10:19.610 --> 10:21.930
<i>Smooth move, Katase-san!</i>

10:21.930 --> 10:25.610
Are you okay, Shinozaki-san? 
Your face is red.

10:23.520 --> 10:25.840
Yes, that's the spirit!

10:25.610 --> 10:30.190
Uh, yes, it's just, 
kinda hot in here, y'know?

10:25.840 --> 10:29.500
Now, Shinozaki-kun just needs to 
do something to thrill Katase-san...

10:31.430 --> 10:34.190
That's it... just a little more...

10:37.190 --> 10:39.320
That was a big meal.

10:39.320 --> 10:42.450
Yeah! And it all was great.

10:43.800 --> 10:48.140
Well, we've got work tomorrow. 
Maybe we should wrap it up for tonight.

10:48.870 --> 10:50.710
Oh, man, it's that late already?

10:51.080 --> 10:55.700
I was hoping we could stay 
a bit longer. That's a shame.

10:57.240 --> 11:00.540
You wanted to stay together... longer?

11:03.620 --> 11:05.740
<i>Does that mean...?</i>

11:06.880 --> 11:08.490
Let me walk you to the station.

11:09.040 --> 11:12.170
Oh, right! Thank you.

11:12.800 --> 11:13.630
Everything okay?

11:13.630 --> 11:14.980
I-It's fine!

11:16.480 --> 11:19.400
<i>What was I thinking...?</i>

11:21.030 --> 11:22.960
Um, Senpai?

11:22.960 --> 11:26.260
Uh, well.. it's... um...

11:28.250 --> 11:30.960
I knew you had it in you, Shinozaki-kun!

11:30.960 --> 11:35.050
Whoa, Manager!
Please don't turn to sugar grains on me!

11:36.350 --> 11:39.870
Thank you for walking me to the station!

11:39.870 --> 11:42.010
See you tomorrow, Senpai!

11:43.060 --> 11:46.550
<i>My Tiny Senpai</i>.

11:54.100 --> 11:56.140
Morning, Shinozaki.

11:56.140 --> 11:57.830
Hey, good morning.

11:58.970 --> 12:00.280
An umbrella?

12:01.110 --> 12:03.530
The weather didn't mention rain, did it?

12:03.530 --> 12:05.400
Oh, this...

12:06.320 --> 12:08.290
<i>Your lucky item today is an umbrella!</i>

12:08.290 --> 12:11.250
Taurus

12:08.290 --> 12:11.290
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hYour lucky item today is an umbrella!

Carry one, and unexpected fortune may find you.

12:08.290 --> 12:11.290
<i>Carry one, and unexpected fortune 
may find you.</i>

12:11.290 --> 12:13.190
So it said.

12:13.190 --> 12:14.360
I see.

12:27.960 --> 12:30.520
Thank goodness I brought an umbrella...

12:37.920 --> 12:41.320
<i>Senpai... Did she not bring an umbrella?</i>

12:42.720 --> 12:43.720
Excuse me!

12:45.260 --> 12:48.250
Would you like to share mine?

12:52.720 --> 12:53.820
Yes!

13:01.600 --> 13:04.160
<i>Sharing an umbrella with Senpai...</i>

13:04.160 --> 13:06.180
<i>Man, this really is lucky!</i>

13:07.310 --> 13:13.210
B-But... I'm so nervous, 
I've barely said anything...

13:16.480 --> 13:19.320
Your shoulder is getting wet, Shinozaki-san.

13:19.960 --> 13:22.980
Oh, I'm sorry if I worried you!

13:25.940 --> 13:27.490
W-Well...

13:27.490 --> 13:30.140
h-how did you end up as my senpai, anyway?

13:30.140 --> 13:31.720
By working at our company first.

13:31.720 --> 13:33.000
That makes sense!

13:33.000 --> 13:35.450
What kind of animals do you like, Senpai?!

13:35.450 --> 13:36.620
Cats!

13:36.620 --> 13:37.750
I knew that!

13:38.220 --> 13:41.280
<i>This is awful! I suck at talking!</i>

13:41.280 --> 13:45.520
Shinozaki-san! You don't have to 
force yourself to talk.

13:45.520 --> 13:48.730
I'm enjoying walking home together as it is.

13:49.760 --> 13:51.550
R-Right...

13:51.550 --> 13:58.520
Come to think of it, you always speak up 
when a meeting gets quiet, don't you?

13:58.520 --> 14:02.250
Yeah. I start to panic 
when no one is talking...

14:02.250 --> 14:05.280
It's even more nerve-wracking 
with the section chief in attendance.

14:05.990 --> 14:10.960
He looks so scary... 
I know he's actually nice, though.

14:06.070 --> 14:13.290
m 0 0 l 80 0 l 80 26 l 0 26

14:06.070 --> 14:13.290
Section Chief

14:06.070 --> 14:13.290
m 0 0 l 80 0 l 80 26 l 0 26

14:06.070 --> 14:13.290
Manager

14:06.070 --> 14:13.290
m 0 0 l 82 0 l 82 26 l 0 26

14:06.070 --> 14:13.290
Design

14:06.070 --> 14:13.290
m 0 0 l 82 0 l 82 26 l 0 26

14:06.070 --> 14:13.290
Planning

14:10.960 --> 14:13.290
I know exactly what you mean!

14:13.740 --> 14:16.720
I wish I knew how to 
get over being so nervous.

14:16.720 --> 14:19.130
I'd hate for it to cause trouble.

14:19.130 --> 14:21.920
You don't need to be so tense about it.

14:21.920 --> 14:25.320
Everybody learns how these 
things work as time goes on.

14:25.320 --> 14:29.080
Besides, the chief has mentioned 
how the way you ask a lot of questions

14:29.080 --> 14:33.120
makes it easier for everyone else to speak up.

14:33.120 --> 14:36.490
Th-That's great to hear.

14:38.420 --> 14:43.150
Oh, sorry, I wanted to stop by the book store 
before heading home, so I'll be going now.

14:43.440 --> 14:46.970
In that case, if you want, 
you can take my umbrella.

14:51.400 --> 14:54.730
I had a great time talking!

14:54.730 --> 14:58.140
Let's give it our all at work again, 
tomorrow, Shinozaki-san.

14:58.690 --> 14:59.740
See you then!

15:03.480 --> 15:05.130
<i>She had one all along?!</i>

15:11.320 --> 15:12.430
Huh?

15:13.110 --> 15:16.330
Is Shinozaki-san taking the day off?

15:16.330 --> 15:19.680
He's sick, apparently. Called in this morning.

15:20.370 --> 15:22.250
Oh, I see...

15:22.690 --> 15:25.450
Your shoulder is getting wet, Shinozaki-kun.

15:25.450 --> 15:27.570
Oh, I'm sorry!

15:29.840 --> 15:30.920
Want to check up on him?

15:30.920 --> 15:32.570
Wh-Why would I do that?!

15:32.570 --> 15:35.080
Well, he is your only kohai, after all!

15:35.080 --> 15:38.080
He's mentioned that living 
on his own is proving to be a handful.

15:49.490 --> 15:51.220
<i>Still not going down...</i>

15:54.800 --> 15:59.930
<i>Well, it's my own fault for going 
into shock in the middle of the rain.</i>

16:05.750 --> 16:07.220
Coming...

16:09.330 --> 16:12.360
How are you feeling, Shinozaki-san?

16:12.730 --> 16:15.680
Senpai?! You went out of your way to visit me?!

16:15.680 --> 16:16.870
Oh, come now.

16:16.870 --> 16:19.770
I was just in the neighborhood.

16:19.770 --> 16:22.460
And you've been out 
for three days, so I was worried,

16:22.460 --> 16:25.720
and I heard living on your own 
was rough for you,

16:25.720 --> 16:26.880
so I brought some supplies.

16:27.230 --> 16:29.880
Thank you so much. That is really thoughtful...

16:38.000 --> 16:40.500
How about I make something for you?

16:50.850 --> 16:52.300
<i>What is even happening...?</i>

16:53.290 --> 16:55.340
<i>I feel crazy-happy.</i>

16:56.810 --> 16:58.490
There you go.

16:58.490 --> 16:59.690
Thank you for the food.

17:00.410 --> 17:01.600
It's good!

17:01.600 --> 17:03.410
I'm glad you like it!

17:03.410 --> 17:06.670
I'll tidy up and do some laundry, too.

17:06.670 --> 17:08.440
Thanks again.

17:08.440 --> 17:10.920
Oh, wait, my underwear!

17:11.440 --> 17:14.760
I really appreciate you doing all this.

17:14.760 --> 17:16.180
Oh, it's all right.

17:16.870 --> 17:20.490
Despite appearances, 
I'm more the big sister type.

17:21.850 --> 17:26.750
<i>I am so, incredibly, crazily happy right now,</i>

17:27.550 --> 17:30.390
<i>I don't even want to get better anymore.</i>

17:33.970 --> 17:38.950
Well, sorry to intrude. Make sure to stay 
warm, and get some more rest, okay?

17:38.950 --> 17:41.640
You're a real life-saver, Senpai.

17:42.120 --> 17:44.810
Come to think of it, what were 
in you in the neighborhood for?

17:44.810 --> 17:46.830
To see a movie with a friend.

17:46.830 --> 17:51.210
Huh? But the theater is in the opposite 
direction of my house from the train station...

17:53.340 --> 17:55.020
W-Well, uh,

17:55.020 --> 17:57.800
I'm running short on time, so...

18:02.440 --> 18:04.600
<i>I messed up...</i>

18:05.050 --> 18:09.100
<i>Maybe I got too excited,
because he's my only kohai.</i>

18:11.110 --> 18:14.920
I guess I'll buy something microwaveable...

18:19.360 --> 18:21.620
Simple, Delicious
Recipe Book!
What to make when someone's sick

18:26.040 --> 18:28.920
Maybe something to cook, too.

18:30.470 --> 18:31.940
<i>Mission accomplished!</i>

18:35.050 --> 18:37.500
A present for Senpai?

18:37.500 --> 18:39.680
Well, it's less a present and more...

18:39.680 --> 18:41.690
A token of my thanks?

18:41.690 --> 18:43.180
Thanks for what?

18:43.180 --> 18:46.600
She came over and looked 
after me when I was sick.

18:46.600 --> 18:48.410
She even cooked for me.

18:48.410 --> 18:51.310
Maybe I should get something 
unobtrusive, like candy.

18:52.270 --> 18:54.220
Are you stupid?!

18:54.220 --> 18:57.870
Why would you give someone who went to your 
house and cooked for you when you were sick

18:57.870 --> 19:01.110
the same gift you'd pass onto 
a business partner for the Bon holiday?!

19:01.520 --> 19:04.120
A business Bon gift?!

19:04.120 --> 19:06.650
Well? Was the food good?

19:06.650 --> 19:08.620
Yeah, very much so.

19:08.620 --> 19:11.530
I-It was downright delicious....

19:11.530 --> 19:13.630
And I think she likes to cook.

19:13.630 --> 19:18.040
Then get her an apron, and say 
"Please come and cook for me again!"

19:18.040 --> 19:20.010
Where did that come from?!

19:20.010 --> 19:23.690
Isn't it considered rude to give 
non-consumables since they take up space?

19:23.690 --> 19:26.910
I say you need to give her something 
that will stick around and remind her of you.

19:26.910 --> 19:29.020
Remind her of what, exactly?!

19:32.130 --> 19:34.020
<i>What should I do?</i>

19:34.020 --> 19:39.280
<i>I ended up actually buying one 
on impulse, but I think...</i>

19:39.280 --> 19:42.620
<i>This might be a lot harder to 
casually hand to her!</i>

19:39.280 --> 19:43.030
m 0 0 l 196 0 l 196 134 l 0 134

19:39.280 --> 19:43.030
<b>Shinozaki's Gift Giving Ease
Ranking!!</b>

19:39.280 --> 19:43.030
1 Souvenirs Snacks
2 Thank-you gifts Snacks
3 Parting gifts Snacks

19:43.750 --> 19:46.030
Maybe I should go with candy after all.

19:46.350 --> 19:48.070
Good morning.

19:48.630 --> 19:51.160
G-G-Good morning, Senpai!

19:51.160 --> 19:54.040
What's wrong? You seem anxious.

19:54.820 --> 19:57.300
Well, it's nothing, really...

19:58.800 --> 20:02.300
<i>Th-The gift! I need to give it to her!</i>

20:02.720 --> 20:05.670
<i>But what if she thinks it's too much?</i>

20:07.000 --> 20:10.280
<i>Then again, I don't think 
Senpai would feel that way...</i>

20:11.310 --> 20:12.710
Excuse me!

20:15.150 --> 20:18.400
Thank you very much for the other day.

20:18.400 --> 20:20.030
I got this for you...

20:26.520 --> 20:30.380
Um... I'm sorry if you don't like it...

20:30.850 --> 20:32.120
An apron?

20:33.810 --> 20:35.670
<i>It's too much, isn't it?!</i>

20:39.610 --> 20:41.450
Thank you so much!

20:42.670 --> 20:45.800
<i>Thank goodness, she seems to like it...</i>

20:45.800 --> 20:47.680
W-Well...

20:49.430 --> 20:51.620
I'm sure you'll look nice in it,

20:52.690 --> 20:54.690
so I hope you'll use it at home.

20:55.700 --> 20:58.410
You wouldn't mind me 
coming by your house again?

20:59.440 --> 21:03.450
I-I meant at your own house, not mine...

21:03.450 --> 21:06.450
Oh, right! That makes sense. Sorry about that.

21:06.780 --> 21:11.290
That was such a silly assumption to make...

21:11.290 --> 21:14.210
Though, if you wouldn't mind, Senpai...

21:15.140 --> 21:18.210
I'd be really glad to have you over again.

21:21.880 --> 21:25.180
Well...  Someday might be nice.

21:25.180 --> 21:27.930
Right, well... whenever is good for you.

21:27.930 --> 21:30.650
You two want the afternoon off?

21:30.650 --> 21:33.020
Manager, give it a rest!
